// Axis delta: texture .linen — a tiled greyscale grain over the page.
//
// Mood-INdependent, unlike accent: a grain is a luminance modulation, so
// it reads on any ground without being re-solved per palette. That is why
// this is one file and the accent is forty-eight.
//
// Alpha 0.06 and scale 7 are the texture's own: a fine grain needs more
// repeats and less weight than a coarse one, or it reads as dirt.
let l0_texture   = "linen"
let l0_texture_a = 0.06
let l0_texture_s = 7
